or neutrals ... but you can _always_ wish for Stormbringer.   btw,
Stormy is flashier than other named weapons but it isn't the greatest,
in my experience.  it does have a good purpose but this can be had in
other ways, equally as effective.

however, to an extent, you can manipulate your alignment.  rumor has it
that there was an awesome chaotic samurai (normally lawful) named Luk No.

i may be confused here but if one finds an unusual helmet you could
consider wearing it backwards ... no, that's not quite right.

without considering askew helmets and with the good fortune of finding
the right altars and the misfortune of crossing your alignment one can
desert ones former alignment for another.

here's an experiment:
kill some _poor_ animal (it should be poor for this to work).  the poor
ones don't usually fight back.  don't eat the corpse (that tends to
be aggravating).  instead, offer the corpse to a god not of your
alignment.  the god of your alignment should be thoroughly disgusted
by now and abandon you.  however, the god whom you've just flattered
may think differently.  if all goes well (wrong?) you'll have changed
alignment.  nuff said ...

